msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:783
msgid "What is stored"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:787
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:787
msgid "eseot_sources, eseot_categories, eseot_post_types and eseot_audit hold your settings; eseot_version records the data version; eseot_show_upgrade_notice flags the one-time notice; eseot_audit_summaries_urls keeps the last 50 summaries for addresses that are not posts, such as the home page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:788
msgid "Post meta"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:788
msgid "_opace_eseot_audit_summary and _opace_eseot_audit_time hold, per audited post, the Pass, Review and Info counts, up to five top Review labels, the five metrics and the time. This feeds the list column and the dashboard widget. Full results are never stored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:789
msgid "Transients"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:789
msgid "Each crawl result is cached for 60 seconds under a key derived from the address, so repeated audits do not hammer the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:793
msgid "What is sent, and when"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:795
msgid "Nothing, until you click a deeper check. The audit runs in your browser against a page served by your own site; the two engines are bundled files, not fetched from a CDN; the crawl check is your server talking to itself; and the summary is saved to your own database over the REST API with a nonce and capability check. Opening a saved tool sends that page address or host to the independent service, in a new tab, under its terms and privacy policy. Opace receives nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:796
msgid "Visitors are never affected. The engines are added to a page only for a logged-in editor with a valid one-off token, and that request is marked noindex and served uncached."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:798
msgid "Uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:800
msgid "Deleting the plugin from the Plugins screen removes every option above, both post meta keys on every post and any cached crawl results, on every site of a network. Deactivating leaves them in place so nothing is lost if you reactivate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:810
msgid "The audit times out or says the page did not report back"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:811
msgid "The hidden frame could not load or could not message the panel within 20 seconds. Usual causes: a security plugin or host header that blocks framing (X-Frame-Options or a Content-Security-Policy frame-ancestors rule), an admin address on a different origin from the front end, a redirect off-site, or a script error on the page. Click Open the page in a new tab; the audit runs there, reports back and the tab closes itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:814
msgid "Metrics are missing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:815
msgid "INP needs a real interaction and is expected to be missing. If other metrics show Not observed, the frame was still loading when the two and a half second capture window closed; click Run again. Check that Capture Web Vitals is ticked on the Audit tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-opace-eseot-help.php:818
msgid "Save the post to get an address"
